# Do not install this package's own optional peerDependencies locally.
#
# `webdriverio` and `@playwright/test` are declared as OPTIONAL peers: they are
# a contract for consumers (this package drives either one via duck-typed
# Page/Browser), not something the repo itself builds or tests against. npm
# still installs a root package's own peers even when optional, which dragged
# the entire webdriverio tree — ~233 packages nothing here imports — into every
# install, and with it a recurring stream of advisories (extract-zip
# GHSA-jmr9-qjv8-65gv, deepmerge-ts GHSA-ggr8-5vv4-36mx) that had to be
# silenced with overrides for code that never runs.
#
# `@playwright/test` is unaffected: it is also a devDependency, so it installs
# on its own merits. The peerDependencies block in package.json is untouched,
# so what consumers see is unchanged.
#
# This file is not published (npm excludes it, and `files` ships only dist/).
omit=peer
